sn47.49:2.3 | S: They meditate observing an aspect of feelings … | T: feelings in feelings …
sn47.49:2.4 | S: mind … | T: mind in mind …
sn47.49:2.5 | S: principles—keen, aware, and mindful, rid of covetousness and displeasure for the world. | T: phenomena in phenomena, ardent, clearly comprehending, mindful, having removed covetousness and displeasure in regard to the world.
sn47.49:2.6 | S: These four kinds of mindfulness meditation should be developed to completely understand these three feelings.” | T: “These four establishments of mindfulness, bhikkhus, are to be developed for the full understanding of these three feelings.”
